NAME
       setsebool - turn SELinux booleans on or off

SYNOPSIS
       setsebool [-P] BOOLEAN on|off
       setsebool [-P] BOOLEAN=VALUE...

DESCRIPTION
       Booleans are switches in the SELinux policy that allow optional
       behaviour, such as httpd_enable_homedirs (Apache may read users'
       public_html directories) or httpd_can_network_connect (Apache may
       open network connections). setsebool changes them.

       Without -P the change lasts only until the next reboot. With -P it is
       also written to the policy store, so it survives reboots. Exam tasks
       almost always want -P. Writing the store takes a few seconds.

       Values can be on/off, 1/0 or true/false. Only root can change
       booleans.

OPTIONS
       -P     Make the change permanent.

EXAMPLES
       Let Apache serve users' home pages, for good:

           setsebool -P httpd_enable_homedirs on
           getsebool httpd_enable_homedirs

       Find booleans about a service:

           getsebool -a | grep ftp
           semanage boolean -l | grep httpd

       Change two at once:

           setsebool -P httpd_can_network_connect=1 httpd_use_nfs=1

SEE ALSO
       getsebool(8), semanage(8), sestatus(8), booleans(8)
